        "--title",
        "comparison launch",
        "An XML element whose tag name equals the configured commentPropName or cdataPropName collides with the synthetic property the parser uses for comments or CDATA in the output object, which can let untrusted input masquerade as parser-generated structure. Add a parser option strictReservedNames (boolean, default true, documented in the TypeScript option type in src/fxp.d.ts). When it is true, encountering an opening tag whose name (after updateTag) equals commentPropName or cdataPropName must throw an Error with the message exactly \"Invalid tag name: <name>\". When it is explicitly set to false, such tags must be parsed as ordinary elements, producing the same output as before this option existed. Source is under src/; tests run with npm test (jasmine).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/."
      ],
